# Twin Wireless social publisher — .gitignore
#
# Added 2026-09-14. THIS REPO IS PUBLIC and had no .gitignore at all, so nothing
# mechanically prevented a live credential from being committed. Nothing
# sensitive was ever tracked (all commits were checked), but the natural act of
# dropping a .env beside post_daily.py to run it locally, then `git add -A`,
# would have published Facebook Page and Instagram tokens to the open internet.

# --- credentials: never, under any name -------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*token*.json
*secret*
credentials*
service-account*.json

# --- customer data / PII ----------------------------------------------------
*.csv
exports/
*customer*
*twilio*

# --- runtime noise ----------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
